.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_pbn" "fuzzygene_pbn"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_pbn \- The qualitative (probabilistic boolean) layer of a trained model: CoD table and rules.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_pbn(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The qualitative (probabilistic boolean) layer of a trained model: CoD table and rules.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained model that was built with \fBpbnRegularization != "none"\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of data.frames
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Returns a named list:
 


 
- \fBcod\fR: one row per (target, regulator) pair, columns \fBtarget\fR / \fBregulator\fR /
 \fBcod\fR / \fBrank\fR; \fBcod\fR is the coefficient of determination of that parent set on the
 binarized matrix, i.e. how much of the boolean state of the target the regulator set
 explains;
- \fBrules\fR: \fBtarget\fR / \fBparents\fR / \fBn_parents\fR / \fBcod\fR, the selected rule of each
 target gene (parents joined by \fB+\fR);
- \fBtargets\fR: \fBtarget\fR / \fBrules\fR / \fBbest_cod\fR, one row per analysed gene;
- \fBsummary\fR: one row with \fBhas_pbn\fR / \fBtargets_analysed\fR / \fBskipped\fR / \fBgenes\fR /
 \fBwarnings\fR.


 


 CoD is a **consistency** measure after binarization, not causal evidence: a rule can have
 a high CoD simply because the target and the parent are both driven by a third gene.
 Use it to suppress pure correlation edges and to report structure uncertainty, not as a
 substitute for perturbation data.
.PP
